<section xml:id="review-questions-2">
  <title>Review Questions</title>

  <p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          The sum of the 2<em>nd</em> and the 4<em>th</em> term of a geometric
          sequence is 10 and the sum of the 3<em>nd</em> and 5<em>th</em> term
          is 20. Find the first term and the common ratio.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <p>
                Given that <m>a_1 = 25</m> and <m>a_n = a_{n-1} + 4</m> for
                <m>n &gt; 1</m>
              </p>

              <p>Find:</p>

              <p>
                <ol>
                  <li>
                    <p><m>a_2, a_3</m>, and <m>a_4</m></p>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <p>a formula for <m>a_n</m> in terms of <m>n</m></p>
                  </li>
                </ol>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>
                Use your formula for <m>a_n</m> to deduce a formula for
                <m>S_n</m>, the sum of the first <m>n</m> terms of the
                sequence <m>a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots a_n</m> and hence find
                <m>S_{10}</m>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          The sum of the three consecutive term of an Arithmetic Progression
          is <m>-3</m> and the product is 24. Find the terms.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          The <m>n</m>th term of an exponential sequence (G.P) is
          <m>2^{1-n}</m>.
        </p>

        <p>Calculate:</p>

        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <p>
                the sum <m>S_n</m>, of the first four terms of the sequence.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>the sum of the sequence to infinity.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Calculate the difference between the sum to infinity of the series
          <m>1 + \frac{1}{3} + \frac{1}{9} + \ldots</m>, and the sum of the
          first 5 terms.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          A sequence defined by <m>U_1 = 2</m>, <m>U_{n+1} = 2U_n - 1</m>,
          <m>n = 2, 3, 4, \ldots</m>
        </p>

        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <p>Find the first five terms of the sequence</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>Show that <m>U_{n+1} = 3U_n - 2U_{n-1}</m></p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          The sum of the 5<em>th</em> and 9<em>th</em> terms of an A.P, is
          <m>-40</m> and and the 11<em>th</em> term is <m>-32</m>. Find the
          first term and the common difference.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          A man's salary is increased by GHc 24 000 each year. His total salary at
          the end of 14 years is GHc 184 000.
        </p>

        <p>Find:</p>

        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <p>his initial salary</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>his salary in the 14<em>th</em> year</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          The sum of the first <m>n</m> terms of a series is given by <m>(n +
          1)^2 - 1</m>. Find the first three terms and an expression in terms
          of <m>n</m> for <m>U_n</m>, <m>(n &gt; 1)</m>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          A tennis ball is released from a height <m>h</m> cm, it rebounds
          one-third of the distance it has fallen after each fall. Find the
          height of;
        </p>

        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <p>the third bounce</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>the <m>n</m>th bounce</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Find the sum of the first <m>n</m> terms of a linear sequence whose
          common difference is 2 is 120 and the sum of the <m>2n</m> term is
          440. Calculate the first term.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Evaluate <m>\sum_{r=1}^{6} (r^2 - 2)</m></p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Renie's outlet manufactures two types of clothing (shirts and
          trousers). The profit is for each shirt and for each pair of
          trousers.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Due to limited resources, the company can produce a combined total
          of no more than 120 pieces. Additionally, to meet demand, they must
          produce at least 20 shirts and 10 pairs of trousers. How many of
          each of the clothing should be produced to make the most profit?
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Find the solution(s) to:</p>

        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <p><m>3x^2 + 5x \ge 2</m>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p><m>x^2 - 2x - 3 \ge 0</m>.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          A company determines that the cost in cedis <m>C</m>, of producing
          <m>m</m> bags of maize is <m>C = 170m + 150</m>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          The revenue <m>R</m>, in cedis, from selling all of the bags of
          maize is <m>R = m^2 + 530</m>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          How many bags of maize should the company produce and sell if the
          company wishes to earn a profit of at least GHc 4 000.00?
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Mr. Buabeng and Ms. Osei run business assembling Hyundai Toyota
          cars.
        </p>

        <p>
          The cost of parts and labour needed for each type of car is shown in
          the table below.
        </p>

        <!-- div center -->

        <tabular>
          <col halign="left"/> <col halign="center"/> <col halign="center"/>
          <row header="yes">
            <cell><term>Car type</term></cell>
            <cell><term>Cost of Parts (<nbsp/>thousand)</term></cell>
            <cell><term>Labour (man-hours)</term></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Hyundai</cell>
            <cell>18</cell>
            <cell>15</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Toyota</cell>
            <cell>36</cell>
            <cell>30</cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <!-- end div center -->

        <p>The business has GHc 150 (thousand) available to buy parts each week.</p>

        <p>
          However, the total labour available each week is 85 man-hours. If
          they make <m>h</m> of Hyundai and <m>t</m> of Toyota each week:
        </p>

        <p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <p>Write down all the inequalities on <m>h</m> and <m>t</m>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>Determine the solution to the set of inequalities.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>
</section>
